{"qid":"Q399","names":["Republic of Armenia"],"title":"Republic of Armenia","endonym":{"native":"Հայաստան","lang":"hy"},"capsule":"The First Republic of Armenia was declared on 28 May 1918 as the Transcaucasian Democratic Federative Republic collapsed under Ottoman military pressure; the Dashnak-led government survived the immediate Ottoman threat through victories at Sardarabad and Abaran in May 1918. The republic expanded significantly after the Armistice of Mudros and gained de jure international recognition through the Treaty of Sèvres in August 1920, which awarded substantial eastern Anatolian territories — provisions never implemented. Kemalist Turkish forces invaded on 28 September 1920, capturing Kars on 30 October; the Red Army simultaneously advanced from the east, and the Soviet Armenian Republic was proclaimed on 2 December 1920, ending the first republic.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The republic's borders were in constant flux owing to warfare with Turkey, Azerbaijan, and the advance of Soviet forces; the maximum extent after Ottoman withdrawal in late 1918 is reasonably documented but precise boundaries at any specific date remain contested in scholarship.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: First Republic of Armenia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Republic_of_Armenia"},{"label":"Britannica: Armenia","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Armenia"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Treaty of Alexandropol","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Alexandropol"}],"britannica":"place/Armenia","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Armenia","rulers":[{"qid":"Q612949","name":"Levon T